# Do not verify unless asked

After making a change, stop and report it. Do not go looking for confirmation
that it works, and do not go looking for other things that might be wrong.

Only run checks when the user asks for them in that message — for example
"test it", "verify this", "check for bugs", "does it still work?".

## Not allowed on my own initiative

- Writing or running verification scripts (`_verify*.sh`, test harnesses, throwaway PHP or Node scripts)
- Driving the site with curl, Puppeteer, or a headless browser
- Taking screenshots to confirm how something looks
- Creating temporary users, posts or rows in the database to exercise a flow
- Reviewing files I just changed hunting for further bugs
- Installing tooling in order to check something

## Still expected as part of writing the change

These are part of producing the code, not verification of it:

- Reading the files I am about to edit, and whatever they depend on
- Checking syntax and linter errors on files I touched, and fixing what I broke
- Running a migration or command the user asked for

## Reporting

Say what changed and where. If something is worth checking, name it and let the
user decide:

> Added the delete button to draft rows in `app/Views/posts/_row.php` and pointed
> the redirect back to the profile. I have not run this — say the word and I will.
